Title bar icon: `.title-icon svg { width: 16px; height: 16px; }` — but the tile gradient is only on icon-tile/tb-tile; title-icon shows the raw glyph on the title bar background — the glyph is white! White glyph on a light title bar = invisible. Options: put a small tile on the title bar too: `<span class="tb-tile title-icon ${app.icon}">`. Use tb-tile (18px) for the title icon. Let me do that: `class="title-icon tb-tile ${app.icon}"`. Then `.title-icon { width: 18px; height: 18px; border-radius: 5px; display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; flex: 0 0 auto; }` and `.tb-tile svg { width: 12px; height: 12px; }`? Hmm, the tile svg size: icon-tile svg 30px; tb-tile svg 12px.

`.tb-tile` base: `display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; flex: 0 0 auto; border-radius: 5px;` size set by context: taskbar 18px, title bar 18px.

Simplify: `.tb-tile { width: 18px; height: 18px; border-radius: 5px; display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; }` and `.tb-tile svg { width: 12px; height: 12px; }`.

For the title: `<span class="title-icon tb-tile ${app.icon}">svg</span>` — good, no extra class needed.

Taskbar button: `display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 7px;`.

Now, `.desktop-icon` is a `<button>` — reset default button styles (font inherit, etc.). Set `font: inherit` and appearance none.

Potential issue: button `dblclick` — fine.

Another consideration: `#windows { pointer-events: none; } .window { pointer-events: auto; }` so empty-area clicks reach the desktop. But wait — desktop's pointerdown handler checks `e.target === desktop || e.target === windowLayer`. With pointer-events none on windowLayer, target can't be windowLayer; it would be desktop. Keep both checks, harmless.

Also `#icons` — clicks on the icons container's padding area would target iconLayer, not an icon; then the selection doesn't get cleared...

