Wait — the `.wallpaper` base has `background-repeat: no-repeat`, but the patterns need repeat! repeating-linear-gradient is fine without repeat (since it's a repeating gradient). Grid and bubbles use background-size and need `background-repeat: repeat`. Fix: set the base to `background-repeat: repeat` — the gradient fills the whole area either way. Actually, with background-size cover and no-repeat, the grid would only show a single 32px cell in the top-left. So the base should be `background-repeat: repeat`. The linear-gradient (aurora/sunset/ocean) without an explicit background-size will stretch to fill the whole element regardless of the repeat setting. So the base is: `background-repeat: repeat;`.

